The Zig reference and C headers are generated from declarations compiled by
the library. A build check rejects stale output. To choose an API, start with
[Choose an API]($link.page('surfaces')); to build a first client, use [Start
building]($link.page('start')).

## The Zig API

The [Zig API reference]($link.page('reference/api')) documents the public
`pancake` module imported by applications. Ownership and lifetime notes live
with the declarations they govern. [The modules]($link.page('modules'))
explains how those declarations are divided by responsibility.

## The C ABI

The C ABI is split into composable archives. Each generated header describes
one archive and includes only the shared definitions it needs.

| Archive | Header | What it carries |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `libpancake_ocapn` | [`pancake_ocapn.h`](https://github.com/jimisaacs/pancake/blob/main/include/pancake_ocapn.h) | shared contexts, frames, values, locators, and URI helpers |
| `libpancake_host` | [`pancake_host.h`](https://github.com/jimisaacs/pancake/blob/main/include/pancake_host.h) | the byte-fed host tier (`pancake_host_*`) |
| `libpancake_driver` | [`pancake_driver.h`](https://github.com/jimisaacs/pancake/blob/main/include/pancake_driver.h) | the native loop; exports only `pancake_driver_*` and adopts a Host from `libpancake_host` through `pancake_driver_take_host` |
| `libpancake_net_transport_tcp` | [`pancake_net_transport_tcp.h`](https://github.com/jimisaacs/pancake/blob/main/include/pancake_net_transport_tcp.h) | the `tcp`, `keyed-tcp`, and `noise-tcp` provider package plus low-level framed cleartext TCP endpoints |
| `libpancake_net_transport_inproc` | [`pancake_net_transport_inproc.h`](https://github.com/jimisaacs/pancake/blob/main/include/pancake_net_transport_inproc.h) | in-process byte pipes, no sockets |
| `libpancake_net_transport_onion` | [`pancake_net_transport_onion.h`](https://github.com/jimisaacs/pancake/blob/main/include/pancake_net_transport_onion.h) | Tor onion services over a daemon you run |
| `libpancake_net_transport_iroh` | [`pancake_net_transport_iroh.h`](https://github.com/jimisaacs/pancake/blob/main/include/pancake_net_transport_iroh.h) | encrypted QUIC; optional, links the Rust sidecar |
| `libpancake_net_transport_webrtc` | [`pancake_net_transport_webrtc.h`](https://github.com/jimisaacs/pancake/blob/main/include/pancake_net_transport_webrtc.h) | peer-to-peer WebRTC DataChannel; optional, links the Rust sidecar |
| `libpancake_net_transport_relay` | [`pancake_net_transport_relay.h`](https://github.com/jimisaacs/pancake/blob/main/include/pancake_net_transport_relay.h) | native `keyed-relay` and end-to-end sealed `noise-relay` provider package |

The driver and transport headers are companions, not supersets: each one
`#include`s `pancake_ocapn.h`, declares only its own family, and expects its
archive to be linked alongside `libpancake_ocapn`.
For the route from a build to a first complete C program, read
[consuming pancake from C](https://github.com/jimisaacs/pancake/blob/main/docs/consuming-from-c.md).
